      "desc:8": "The §3CO2 Scrubber§r is a mechanism for cleaning air in sealed environments under increased pressure.\n\nThe device absorbs §bCarbon Dioxide§r from the surrounding air and collects it. It only works if two conditions are met: the room is sealed and isolated, and the air pressure is elevated (above 1.0 atm). The latter can be achieved by adding a stream of §bOxygen§r from the ventilation to the Earth\u0027s air (resulting in a total pressure of 1.1 atm).\n\n§2The maximum number of scrubbers in a room is 5; any additional units placed will not collect carbon dioxide.§r",
